"""character roster: ownership off builds

`DESIGN_character_roster.md` §3. Ownership was a boolean on `builds`, which cannot hold it: a
user may own several builds of one character (`uq_builds_owner_character` was dropped by owner
decision, 2026-08-24), so the fact has as many stored answers as there are builds and no correct
way to reduce them — and twelve characters the owner owns have no build at all, because a build
is only made for a character holding gear. It moves to its own composite-keyed table where a
character has exactly one answer per user.

**Hand-written, not autogenerated.** `--autogenerate` against the dev database also proposed a
type change on `optimization_runs.visibility` and an index beside it — pre-existing drift that
has nothing to do with this change, and folding it in would make the revision mean two things.

Revision ID: bbf8c576ecfa
Revises: aa024ff55891
Create Date: 2026-09-03 17:10:26.529195

"""
